module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_call_resolving_to_a_coproduct_arm_node_renders_as_unit

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_call_resolving_to_a_coproduct_arm_node_renders_as_unit: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_call_resolving_to_a_coproduct_arm_node_renders_as_unit" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a call whose declared result is a coproduct (directly or through an alias chain) resolves to the coproduct's ARM node instead of the applied CARRIER. Measured in the v1 seed's emitted output during the fold-accumulator inference work (gunbc#16212 follow-up, session bold-stag-227, 2026-11-11): `list_snoc_item`'s fold step calls `list_snoc`, whose declared result is `FreeMonoid<T>` (a coproduct: Nil | Cons), and the resolved type carried by the call is the `Cons` arm node itself -- a node with the coproduct's parameter count and the arm payload as children -- where the call's type should be the carrier `FreeMonoid` applied to the element type. The arm node is not a type: it is a declaration-internal member shape. Any consumer that reads it as a type gets a wrong answer, and two consumers silently agreed to be wrong in different ways.",
    "HOW IT HID: the emitter's type-leaf renderer `gunbc.v1.compiler.emit_rust.rust_render_type_leaf_name` (src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag, the `TypeLeafIsValueVariantOf` arm) renders a value-variant node in type position as `()` -- correct for the Rust projection of an enum VARIANT value, silent nonsense for an arm node that reached a TYPE position by mistake. So the wrong resolved type never surfaced as a refusal: it surfaced downstream as rustc E0308 in the EMITTED v2 output, `type mismatch` where `()` had been rendered for what should have been `FreeMonoid<Rc<Node>>` (observed at emitted v2_std_grammar.rs:983 during the inference census, with the fold accumulator annotated `Witness<()>` while the arms built `Witness<Rc<Node>>` payloads). The other consumer, the fold-accumulator refinement `gunbc.v1.compiler.infer.refine_fold_acc_from_step_return`, reads the step lambda's return type; an arm-shaped return is neither a resolved fact nor a refusable shape, so it adopted it as an accumulator annotation -- fabricating `Witness<()>`. The v1-side guards that decline such shapes at the synthesis and join seams land with the fold-accumulator inference work in the gunbc#16134 lane (filed separately from this row); they decline the wrong answer at two seams, they do not correct it at its source, which is where this row's trigger sits.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (a wrong resolved type rendered as a plausible `()` and adopted as an annotation, silently). CEILING: reachable now. The call site's target resolution has the declaration in hand when it builds the call type; mapping a coproduct (or an alias chain ending in one) to the applied carrier, with the declaration's generic arguments, is the same carrier application every other type reference performs. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: (a) the v1 resolution/inferencer site that hands a call whose declared result is a coproduct the ARM node -- the walk from `list_snoc_item`'s call through the `FreeMonoid` alias chain, upstream of `gunbc.v1.compiler.infer` where call types are attached -- returns the applied carrier instead; and (b) `rust_render_type_leaf_name` refuses an arm node reaching a type position with a typed, located diagnostic (`compile_error!` emission) instead of rendering `()`, so no future producer can hide behind the renderer. A claim must go red at (a) by asserting the call's resolved type is the applied carrier `FreeMonoid<T>` (not the Cons arm), and red at (b) by authoring a program whose type position is fed an arm node and asserting the refusal text. Both reds must be independent of the fold-accumulator guards above, which stay as the decline-at-the-seam controls. Owner unassigned at filing.",
    "CLIMB RECEIPT: pending. Filed by gunbc#16212's fold-accumulator inference work, which fixed the ADOPTION of arm-shaped evidence (decline at the synthesis and join seams, fail-closed per gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed) but not its PRODUCTION; this row carries the production defect until the trigger lands.",
    "SECOND MEASUREMENT, SAME PRODUCTION PATH (fold-result formals, session bold-stag-227, 2026-11-12): a fold whose step body constructs a payload into a constructor arm of the accumulator's own carrier (`match acc { Absent => ..., Present { value: RejectedUrl { .. } } }` over `Option<T>`) resolves the fold CALL's type argument to the ARM node `Present` (children = the one payload field) instead of the applied carrier `Option<RejectedUrl>` -- the coproduct case of this row, now measured a second way. Its downstream blast radius, all from the one wrong resolved type: the join of the step arms mis-pairs a child against the carrier's formal and refuses (`arms return two different types` on a fold whose arms agree); the emitter's arm-in-type-position renderer turns the arm node into `()` (E0308 in emitted output); and the fold-accumulator annotation falls back to `_` (E0282). The synthesis-evidence and join-adoption guards travel with that same #16134-lane work, not with this row: once they are in, nothing adopts arm-shaped evidence, and no fold is annotated from it.",
    "NAMED RESIDUE (ruled by warm-bear-654, 2026-11-12, do not widen): a join that refuses keeps the legacy positional fallback -- `first_live_branch_value_type` takes the first live arm, the ExprMatch value fold keeps the LEFT arm, `join_or_prefer` keeps the legacy `prefer_specific_type` pick. No preference pick may be added beside a refused join: refinement of a free position by an instantiated one lives in `join_type_nodes_opt` only (carrier identity plus pairwise argument list). TRIGGER for retiring the positional fallbacks: turn a still-refused join into a typed, located refusal once the three-population census shows the population can bear it (every remaining refusal enumerated and correction-shaped).",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust", decl_name: "emit_rust_fold_method_call"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust", decl_name: "render_rust_type_without_applied_binding"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "refine_fold_acc_from_step_return"),
  ],
}
